# Typed into the Go console of go-uefi.img on q35 with no PS/2 controller,
# through a USB keyboard behind a hub (make usb-smoke-hub, W28-S02): the
# hardware report's USB lines, a file from the stick on the hub's third
# port, a program, mousetest with the mouse behind the second hub; the
# stick pulled from the hub and plugged back (QEMU's monitor; QEMU deletes
# a -drive with its device, so the second plug is a second drive), found
# again as the next ub disk and in the report; then poweroff.
wait burrow>
type hw
key ret
wait mounts:
type cat /mnt/hello.txt
key ret
wait Hello from the FAT32
type run /bin/hello
key ret
wait hello from ring 3
type run /bin/mousetest
key ret
wait right click ends
mouse 100 50
click left
wait left down at
click right
wait mousetest: done
wait burrow>
monitor device_del stickdev
wait disconnected
monitor device_add usb-storage,bus=xhci.0,port=1.3,drive=stick2,id=stickdev2
wait storage ubb
type hw
key ret
wait irq 1
type poweroff
key ret
